	"metadata.name": "Kluonoa",
	"metadata.tips": "\"Swimsuit?\"\n\"Right, swimsuit.\" Kluonoa insists that the core function of a swimsuit isn't swimming — it's \"letting the water know you're ready.\" \"If you go into the water without a swimsuit, the water gets angry,\" she once explained in all seriousness, \"and then it'll sink you on purpose.\" — This theory has zero scientific backing to date, but she remains utterly convinced.",
